My first Monk ascention - very cool!

Some notable stuff:

I got 3 wishes from thrones.

In the mid-game my dog became a mastodon, and he went on to cheerfully butt
everything we met into oblivion, until he was gulped by a trapper.  I was
angy with myself for letting him fight a trapper, so I got another pet and
went back to my poly trap.  On the first try - another mastodon!  This one
made it to Medusa, where he valiently fell to a stone gollum.  After medusa
I don't use pets anyway.

Later, I spent about six hours looking for Vlad's stairway, until I realized
it can exist on a fixed map (Orcus town).

This is the first time I've ever wished for an Artifact - got the Staff of
Aesc..(mumble mumble) which in my mind is way too powerful.  But for my
first Monk I was taking no chances.  Genocided L's, I rarely genocide
either.

I died once from disintegration.  The only intrinsic I gained from eating
was disintegration (from the same dragon that killed me).

I think if you have weaponless conduct the game should prompt you before
using a pickaxe as a weapon.  It's not as though you would accidentally
attack something with a pickaxe if you didn't want to.  This is along the
same lines as when you could kill your pet before safepet became an option.

I didn't use a weapon at all until I got the castle and wished for the Staff
of A.

I lost 3 (!) separate robes from blasts of various types, and two T-shirts
that were up to +5.  Finally I went to Ludios and made 4 more Hawaiian
shirts and kept a few spares.  The Eyes were my only source of magic
resistance.

I don't play for score, but I collect gems and gold anyway.  I forgot a
stashpile somewhere, which contained my ?'s of gold detection and untold
loot.  I had a demonbane there but I never did find it.  I should have taken
notes.
